{"id":390464489,"author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"node_id":"RE_kwDORi26-c4XRgPp","tag_name":"v0.8.46","target_commitish":"main","name":"v0.8.46","draft":false,"immutable":false,"prerelease":false,"created_at":"2026-09-17T05:48:54Z","updated_at":"2026-09-17T05:52:44Z","published_at":"2026-09-17T05:52:44Z","assets":[],"body":"# HyperFrames v0.8.46\n\nReleased on 2026-09-17.\n\nEngine motion blur picks its own sample count per frame now, instead of one fixed count for a whole render.\n\n## Features\n\n- **Engine:** The sub-frame motion blur added in v0.8.45 used a fixed sample count for every frame of a render (16 by default). That undersamples fast or hard-edged motion and oversamples content that barely moves. The engine now measures how much a frame actually moved before choosing how many samples it gets, between 16 and 64, so quality goes up where it was undersampled instead of being spent evenly on every frame. Frames that need the extra accuracy cost more to render; a frame whose only change is a fade or a colour shift skips the measurement step and stays at the old cost. Nothing changes if `samplesPerFrame` is set explicitly ([2ab7b8686](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/commit/2ab7b8686870cb435674e20d48b4100db2fa2052), [#4031](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/pull/4031)).\n\n## Full changelog\n\nhttps://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/compare/v0.8.45...v0.8.46\n","reactions":{"total_count":3,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0}}
